# Interaction-ledger captures. One image per click per tuple is 160 files and
# 26 MB, regenerated by one command and replaced on every re-record, so committing
# them would add that much to every clone of a public repository each time. What
# IS committed is the ledger JSON, which records each capture's SHA-256 beside the
# transition it belongs to: the hash is the tamper-evident part, and the images are
# reproduced with `node scripts/ui-evidence/interaction-ledger.mjs`.
docs/interface/ledger/shots-*/
# Fetched from the public dim sum catalog and downscaled; never committed here.
/public/dim-sum/
